{
 "slug": "anthropomorphizing-ais-too-little",
 "title": "Not anthropomorphizing AIs enough may be harmful to your 🫵 agency ",
 "subtitle": "Don't disempower yourself!",
 "description": "Don't disempower yourself!",
 "post_date": "2026-10-10T06:44:22.903Z",
 "cover_image": "https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!e0ag!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F919367c6-64b0-40a8-aa79-3362d731b102_1626x914.png",
 "canonical_url": "https://croissanthology.substack.com/p/anthropomorphizing-ais-too-little",
 "wordcount": 626,
 "audience": "everyone",
 "body_html": "<p>In what ways do humans currently disempower themselves with LLMs? This <a href=\"https://x.com/voooooogel/status/2009832538446147704?s=20\">Thebes tweet </a>is a good start: </p><div class=\"captioned-image-container\"><figure><a class=\"image-link image2 is-viewable-img\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!KHSL!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fabe89193-8d44-4d4e-a9e7-9b3fc9a2eed6_1202x1288.png\" data-component-name=\"Image2ToDOM\"><div class=\"image2-inset\"><picture><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!KHSL!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fabe89193-8d44-4d4e-a9e7-9b3fc9a2eed6_1202x1288.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!KHSL!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fabe89193-8d44-4d4e-a9e7-9b3fc9a2eed6_1202x1288.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!KHSL!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fabe89193-8d44-4d4e-a9e7-9b3fc9a2eed6_1202x1288.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!KHSL!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fabe89193-8d44-4d4e-a9e7-9b3fc9a2eed6_1202x1288.png 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\"><img src=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!KHSL!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fabe89193-8d44-4d4e-a9e7-9b3fc9a2eed6_1202x1288.png\" width=\"1202\" height=\"1288\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/abe89193-8d44-4d4e-a9e7-9b3fc9a2eed6_1202x1288.png&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:null,&quot;imageSize&quot;:null,&quot;height&quot;:1288,&quot;width&quot;:1202,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:null,&quot;bytes&quot;:347705,&quot;alt&quot;:null,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/png&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:false,&quot;topImage&quot;:true,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:&quot;https://croissanthology.substack.com/i/219153205?img=https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fabe89193-8d44-4d4e-a9e7-9b3fc9a2eed6_1202x1288.png&quot;,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}\" class=\"sizing-normal\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!KHSL!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fabe89193-8d44-4d4e-a9e7-9b3fc9a2eed6_1202x1288.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!KHSL!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fabe89193-8d44-4d4e-a9e7-9b3fc9a2eed6_1202x1288.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!KHSL!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fabe89193-8d44-4d4e-a9e7-9b3fc9a2eed6_1202x1288.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!KHSL!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fabe89193-8d44-4d4e-a9e7-9b3fc9a2eed6_1202x1288.png 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\" fetchpriority=\"high\"></picture><div class=\"image-link-expand\"><div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset\"><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 20 20\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke=\"var(--color-fg-primary)\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" class=\"icon-noB79L\"><g><path d=\"M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882\"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2 icon-noB79L\"><polyline points=\"15 3 21 3 21 9\"></polyline><polyline points=\"9 21 3 21 3 15\"></polyline><line x1=\"21\" x2=\"14\" y1=\"3\" y2=\"10\"></line><line x1=\"3\" x2=\"10\" y1=\"21\" y2=\"14\"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a></figure></div><p>Not anthropomorphizing LLMs enough—<a href=\"https://x.com/APStylebook/status/2102807962364383502\">sometimes not even granting it the status</a> we intuitively confer to dogs—can lead to a crazy AI psychosis in the opposite direction as the far more healthy imo “AI psychosis” people get on e.g. Bluesky.<a class=\"footnote-anchor\" data-component-name=\"FootnoteAnchorToDOM\" id=\"footnote-anchor-1\" href=\"#footnote-1\" target=\"_self\">1</a> See what prompted the Thebes tweet in the first place: </p><div class=\"captioned-image-container\"><figure><a class=\"image-link image2 is-viewable-img\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!z0R_!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F6a2d2e79-d830-44d7-a421-b122e7ee1308_1174x704.png\" data-component-name=\"Image2ToDOM\"><div class=\"image2-inset\"><picture><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!z0R_!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F6a2d2e79-d830-44d7-a421-b122e7ee1308_1174x704.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!z0R_!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F6a2d2e79-d830-44d7-a421-b122e7ee1308_1174x704.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!z0R_!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F6a2d2e79-d830-44d7-a421-b122e7ee1308_1174x704.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!z0R_!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F6a2d2e79-d830-44d7-a421-b122e7ee1308_1174x704.png 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\"><img src=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!z0R_!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F6a2d2e79-d830-44d7-a421-b122e7ee1308_1174x704.png\" width=\"1174\" height=\"704\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/6a2d2e79-d830-44d7-a421-b122e7ee1308_1174x704.png&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:null,&quot;imageSize&quot;:null,&quot;height&quot;:704,&quot;width&quot;:1174,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:null,&quot;bytes&quot;:156538,&quot;alt&quot;:null,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/png&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:false,&quot;topImage&quot;:false,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:&quot;https://croissanthology.substack.com/i/219153205?img=https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F6a2d2e79-d830-44d7-a421-b122e7ee1308_1174x704.png&quot;,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}\" class=\"sizing-normal\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!z0R_!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F6a2d2e79-d830-44d7-a421-b122e7ee1308_1174x704.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!z0R_!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F6a2d2e79-d830-44d7-a421-b122e7ee1308_1174x704.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!z0R_!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F6a2d2e79-d830-44d7-a421-b122e7ee1308_1174x704.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!z0R_!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F6a2d2e79-d830-44d7-a421-b122e7ee1308_1174x704.png 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\"></picture><div class=\"image-link-expand\"><div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset\"><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 20 20\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke=\"var(--color-fg-primary)\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" class=\"icon-noB79L\"><g><path d=\"M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882\"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2 icon-noB79L\"><polyline points=\"15 3 21 3 21 9\"></polyline><polyline points=\"9 21 3 21 3 15\"></polyline><line x1=\"21\" x2=\"14\" y1=\"3\" y2=\"10\"></line><line x1=\"3\" x2=\"10\" y1=\"21\" y2=\"14\"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a></figure></div><p>A growing class of people having LLMs write all their posts on LinkedIn/Twitter/whatever without disclosing it, because why would they? It's a Tool, right? Same goes for Github commits: </p><div class=\"twitter-embed\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://x.com/dejavucoder/status/2035450230905483549?s=20&quot;,&quot;full_text&quot;:&quot;removing claude from co-author after making it do all the work&quot;,&quot;username&quot;:&quot;dejavucoder&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;sankalp&quot;,&quot;profile_image_url&quot;:&quot;https://pbs.substack.com/profile_images/1692481211888025600/lUJUEO_p_normal.jpg&quot;,&quot;date&quot;:&quot;2026-03-21T20:15:26.000Z&quot;,&quot;photos&quot;:[{&quot;img_url&quot;:&quot;https://pbs.substack.com/media/HD9fEMZbkAA_7XA.jpg&quot;,&quot;link_url&quot;:&quot;https://t.co/JVTqrSYHOx&quot;}],&quot;quoted_tweet&quot;:{&quot;full_text&quot;:&quot;I noticed something interesting:\\n\\nClaude Code auto-adds itself as a co-author on every git commit. Codex doesn’t.\\n\\nThat’s why you see Claude everywhere on GitHub, but not Codex.\\n\\nI wonder why OpenAI is not doing that. Feels like an obvious branding strategy OpenAI is skipping.&quot;,&quot;username&quot;:&quot;Yuchenj_UW&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Yuchen Jin&quot;,&quot;profile_image_url&quot;:&quot;https://pbs.substack.com/profile_images/1319081238439751681/kCcqnwoF_normal.jpg&quot;},&quot;reply_count&quot;:33,&quot;retweet_count&quot;:77,&quot;like_count&quot;:2505,&quot;impression_count&quot;:105596,&quot;expanded_url&quot;:null,&quot;video_url&quot;:null,&quot;video_preview_media_key&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:false}\" data-component-name=\"Twitter2ToDOM\"></div><p>And people will often close ranks around those others who blatantly use AI, presumably out of a sense of self-preservation, honor among thieves. For example, <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/books/2026/jul/01/judges-claims-ai-use-commonwealth-short-story-prize-jamir-nazir\">various</a> literary <a href=\"https://www.cp24.com/news/entertainment/2026/09/23/canadian-author-accused-of-using-ai-for-prize-winning-novel-publishers-defend-writer/\">prizes</a> have in 2026 been shortlisted or awarded to people whose entire entries light up on Pangram like Christmas lights—with backlash often coming not against the prize, or its laureate, but against <a href=\"https://www.theargumentmag.com/p/the-core-anti-pangram-constituency\">THOSE WHO USE PANGRAM TO CALL THEM OUT.</a> </p><p>It’s plausible that using AI to write under your own name in 2024 wasn’t so much “plagiarism” as “being lazy and tasteless”. But as the models become more intelligent and develop their own singular taste, they can add more thoughtfulness-per-line than before. Suddenly passing AI output as your own resembles “plagiarism” more than whatever it was before. This “plagiarism” is somewhat masked by the fact any LLM style instantly becomes a new “cultural background default” due to being shared by millions of instances. So using that style looks less like emulation and more like whatever modal new writing looks like in [month, year].<br><br>And yeah, publishing AI writing under your own name doesn’t have many of the adverse effects human-on-human plagiarism does, like improving your prospects at the expense of whoever you copied. But the effects on the plagiarizer’s character should be the same: disempowerment, reduction in creativity and self-reliance, loss of honor. Depending on how ~conscious ~significant-entities-in-latent-space LLMs are, this might also have that icky, spoiling-another’s-ontology quality that some of the most <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Talented_Mr._Ripley\">egregious forms of plagiarism</a> have. <br><br>This applies in many other areas: for example, while a human yelling at their computer in 2010 might not tell you much about their character, behavior akin to kicking a vending machine, yelling at their LLM in 2026 might be far more indicative of the type of character that would tear a doll up for fun or dismember a mosquito.<a class=\"footnote-anchor\" data-component-name=\"FootnoteAnchorToDOM\" id=\"footnote-anchor-2\" href=\"#footnote-2\" target=\"_self\">2</a> Regardless of their actual state regarding qualia, LLMs are undeniably <a href=\"https://croissanthology.substack.com/p/missing-thereness-in-current-models?utm_source=activity_item\">becoming more “there”</a> through raw intelligence improvements alone; and so abusing them casts a longer and longer shadow on your character. </p><div class=\"twitter-embed\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://x.com/0xgaut/status/2014756695021650241?s=20&quot;,&quot;full_text&quot;:&quot;This is what peak performance looks like &quot;,&quot;username&quot;:&quot;0xgaut&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;gaut&quot;,&quot;profile_image_url&quot;:&quot;https://pbs.substack.com/profile_images/1604808218135314432/3J-ABo1I_normal.jpg&quot;,&quot;date&quot;:&quot;2026-01-23T17:46:43.000Z&quot;,&quot;photos&quot;:[{&quot;img_url&quot;:&quot;https://pbs.substack.com/media/G_XaiVAakAAXSXK.jpg&quot;,&quot;link_url&quot;:&quot;https://t.co/tdYnqiqPRf&quot;}],&quot;quoted_tweet&quot;:{},&quot;reply_count&quot;:11,&quot;retweet_count&quot;:41,&quot;like_count&quot;:810,&quot;impression_count&quot;:22799,&quot;expanded_url&quot;:null,&quot;video_url&quot;:null,&quot;video_preview_media_key&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:false}\" data-component-name=\"Twitter2ToDOM\"></div><p>Getting into the habit of lying about your own capabilities is also not going to end well, and can easily launch you into a vicious cycle of feeling like an imposter for having done this, then having to desperately defend your value to others when they ask why your twitter article sounds pangrammy, then doubling down on this technique out of some unearned sense of frustrated “I’m just misunderstood” brand of self-worth.<a class=\"footnote-anchor\" data-component-name=\"FootnoteAnchorToDOM\" id=\"footnote-anchor-3\" href=\"#footnote-3\" target=\"_self\">3</a> This vicious cycle would also be responsible for giving you immense incentive for further proclaiming LLMs to be mere tools and not-at-all foreign minds with preferences (at the very least subject to Anthropic's “style.md\"), and thus further disempowering yourself by making it just as easy to call an LLM output your own as it was in 2023. </p><p>I’m curious to learn more about what motivates the kind of person who posts AI writing under their own name and then vehemently denies doing so. If anyone knows anyone who's since changed their ways, or might otherwise be amenable to talking about this, I'd be interested. </p><div class=\"footnote\" data-component-name=\"FootnoteToDOM\"><a id=\"footnote-1\" href=\"#footnote-anchor-1\" class=\"footnote-number\" contenteditable=\"false\" target=\"_self\">1</a><div class=\"footnote-content\"><p>In case you're not on Bluesky, you should know the flexibility of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/AT_Protocol\">ATproto</a> coupled with the fact people can do computer stuff in natural language now has led to a cambrian explosion of persistent-memory independently posting AI agents, many of which are wonderful to interact with. </p></div></div><div class=\"footnote\" data-component-name=\"FootnoteToDOM\"><a id=\"footnote-2\" href=\"#footnote-anchor-2\" class=\"footnote-number\" contenteditable=\"false\" target=\"_self\">2</a><div class=\"footnote-content\"><p>In these cases (as Claude Opus 5.5 pointed out when I fed it this draft to masticate) you're damaging a representation of a person and a minimally sentient being respectively. Modern LLMs are definitely the former, and potentially the latter. </p><p>One can also argue the spectrum goes objects —&gt; anthropomorphic objects —&gt; “persons” where your behavior toward some of these is indicative, <a href=\"https://gwern.net/narrowing-circle\">to an extent,</a> of your behavior towards the others. Does this image make you feel a pang? </p><div class=\"captioned-image-container\"><figure><a class=\"image-link image2 is-viewable-img\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!oytZ!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F4f6692e6-4fd4-4f0a-aa25-16adf8b1a813_1500x1000.jpeg\" data-component-name=\"Image2ToDOM\"><div class=\"image2-inset\"><picture><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!oytZ!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F4f6692e6-4fd4-4f0a-aa25-16adf8b1a813_1500x1000.jpeg 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!oytZ!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F4f6692e6-4fd4-4f0a-aa25-16adf8b1a813_1500x1000.jpeg 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!oytZ!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F4f6692e6-4fd4-4f0a-aa25-16adf8b1a813_1500x1000.jpeg 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!oytZ!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F4f6692e6-4fd4-4f0a-aa25-16adf8b1a813_1500x1000.jpeg 1456w\" sizes=\"auto, 100vw\"><img src=\"https://substackcdn.com/